@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+Feature: DOM stability during state changes
+  As a browser-based user
+  I want the todo list to mutate existing DOM nodes when state changes
+  So that script references to elements remain valid after interaction
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Toggling a todo mutates the existing node in-place
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo preserves the item's DOM node
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk", "Walk dog", "Write code"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox on the "Buy milk" item
+    Then the "Buy milk" item should have the completed class
+    And the "Buy milk" item element is the same DOM node as before the toggle
+    And the "Walk dog" item element is the same DOM node as before the toggle
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a completed todo back to active preserves the node
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk", "Walk dog"
+    And "Walk dog" is completed
+    When I click the toggle checkbox on the "Walk dog" item
+    Then the "Walk dog" item should not have the completed class
+    And the "Walk dog" item element is the same DOM node as before the toggle
+    And the "Buy milk" item element is the same DOM node as before the toggle
+
+  Rule: Toggle-all mutates each item's node in-place
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all completed preserves all item DOM nodes
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk", "Walk dog", "Write code"
+    When I click the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then all todos should be marked as completed
+    And each item element is the same DOM node as before the toggle-all
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all active preserves all item DOM nodes
+    Given all todos are completed
+    When I click the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then all todos should be active
+    And each item element is the same DOM node as before the toggle-all
+
+  Rule: Clear completed preserves remaining item nodes
+
+  Scenario: Clearing completed preserves remaining items' DOM nodes
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk", "Walk dog", "Write code"
+    And "Buy milk" is completed
+    And "Write code" is completed
+    When I click the clear-completed button
+    Then the todo list should contain 1 item
+    And the "Walk dog" item element is the same DOM node as before clear
+
+  @conformance
+  Scenario: The render method must mutate existing nodes rather than rebuilding
+    Given the source at "js/app.js"
+    When the verifier checks the render method
+    Then the todo list is not rebuilt via innerHTML replacement during toggle, toggle-all, or clear-completed operations
\ No newline at end of file
